  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate the velocity function by differentiating the position function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{log}_{2}\u2061t-2t) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the velocity at $t=2,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the velocity function above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =\\frac{3}{2\\operatorname{ln}\u20612}-2 \\\\  & =0.16404\u2026 \\\\  & \u22480.2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
